## Open-source status: BLOCKED, and this is the reason

Four files are substantially derived from statonjr/glimmer-ios-demo, whose
notebooks this project's own `tools/extract-from-notebooks` reads:

    https://github.com/statonjr/glimmer-ios-demo
    verified at 5c7eeb8, 2026-09-03

**That repository carries no licence file**, at any path, on that ref.

Measured, so the size of the problem is known rather than guessed. Counting
substantive lines, comments and blank lines excluded:

| our file | lines | also in the demo | of those, also in your MIT glitter-uikit |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| `src/raylib/host.clj`    | 170 | 130 |  0 |
| `src/raylib/gallery.clj` | 315 |  83 |  0 |
| `src/raylib/touch.clj`   |  35 |  35 |  0 |
| `src/raylib/link.clj`    |  16 |  16 |  1 |
| `src/raylib/probe.clj`   |  53 |   2 |  1 |
| `src/raylib/objc.clj`    |  32 |  13 | 13 |

The last two rows are already clear. `objc.clj` shares only lines that are also
in glitter-uikit's own `ffi.clj`, which is MIT and ours, so its provenance runs
straight to that rather than through the demo. `probe.clj` was written here.
`src/raylib/scenes/*.cljc` and `src/poc/**` are clean too, being MIT from jasalt
and zlib from raylib-jlt.

That leaves **264 lines across four files** as the whole of the problem. With no licence, the default is
ordinary copyright: all rights reserved, and no permission to copy, modify or
redistribute. So this project cannot be published, relicensed or moved to an
organisation as it stands, however small the diff or generous the intent.

Three ways forward, in the order they should be tried:

1. **Ask.** A request to add MIT or zlib upstream resolves it completely, costs
   the author nothing, and is the only option that keeps the attribution
   honest. The demo is itself built on glitter and glitter-uikit, both MIT and
   both ours, and it says so warmly throughout its README. Someone writing a
   demo of your libraries is about as likely to say yes as anyone gets. A draft
   of the request is in `docs/announcements/licence-request.md`.
2. **Rewrite those four files** from the public facts rather than from the
   notebooks: SDL's `docs/README-ios.md`, raylib's headers, Apple's docs, and
   this project's own device measurements. 264 lines, and the two smallest are
   near-mechanical, `link.clj` being four `defcfn` declarations of published SDL
   symbols. `host.clj` is the real work, though we now understand that loop
   better than the notebooks do, having fixed its frame timing and refuted its
   framebuffer claim on hardware.
3. **Stay private.** No obligation is breached by a private repository, and
   this is the status quo.

Note that the demo's own use of glitter-uikit does not itself settle this.
MIT is a grant, not a trade: it lets him build on our work without obliging him
to license his own back. It makes option 1 very likely to land. It is not a
substitute for it.

Until one of those is done, treat this repository as private and unpublishable.
The presence of a LICENSE file does not change that: a licence grants what the
grantor holds, and this is the one part we do not hold.
